{:edb/db-before-t 2050 :edb/db-after-t 2051 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535363 50 #inst "2026-10-08T22:48:30.356Z" 13194139535363 true] [17592186119876 1020 #edb/ref 17592186345925 13194139535363 true] [17592186119876 1020 #edb/ref 17592186345928 13194139535363 true] [17592186119877 1020 #edb/ref 17592186345911 13194139535363 true] [17592186119877 1020 #edb/ref 17592186345935 13194139535363 true] [17592186119878 1020 #edb/ref 17592186345918 13194139535363 true] [17592186345911 1017 #edb/ref 17592186345912 13194139535363 true] [17592186345911 1089 "q-107038" 13194139535363 true] [17592186345911 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535363 true] [17592186345911 1100 "Find the vertical asymptotes of $f(x)=\\frac{(x+2)({x}^{4}+{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2})}{{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}}.$" 13194139535363 true] [17592186345911 1113 #uuid "ffff2c65-4914-5cab-92fb-8939605d9866" 13194139535363 true] [17592186345911 1145 "Let's simplify the expression by factoring both the numerator and the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x+2)({x}^{4}+{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2})}{{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}(x+2)({x}^{2}+x-6)}{{x}^{2}(x+2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{{x}^{2}(x+2)}({x}^{2}+x-6)}{\\cancel{{x}^{2}(x+2)}} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}+x-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the denominator is never zero, we conclude that this function has no vertical asymptotes. A plot of the function is below. Note that it is not defined at $x=-2$ and $x=0.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063519/assets/31f16682ad863f5f320130705ac57415a74340f3fe73a67a03b4df258c2577e7.png)" 13194139535363 true] [17592186345912 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345913 13194139535363 true] [17592186345912 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345914 13194139535363 true] [17592186345912 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345915 13194139535363 true] [17592186345912 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345916 13194139535363 true] [17592186345912 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345917 13194139535363 true] [17592186345912 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535363 true] [17592186345912 1041 "selection" 13194139535363 true] [17592186345912 1104 #edb/ref 17592186345913 13194139535363 true] [17592186345912 1110 #uuid "8a440378-c4e7-5e4d-8eef-4099ec5e60ea" 13194139535363 true] [17592186345913 1034 "No vertical asymptotes" 13194139535363 true] [17592186345913 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535363 true] [17592186345913 1111 #uuid "fdf2b4ff-1f6a-5796-97ce-063614d38def" 13194139535363 true] [17592186345914 1034 "x=2" 13194139535363 true] [17592186345914 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535363 true] [17592186345914 1111 #uuid "f5428b4f-1422-5ae9-bf92-05116eae053a" 13194139535363 true] [17592186345915 1034 "x=0" 13194139535363 true] [17592186345915 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535363 true] [17592186345915 1111 #uuid "cef396a3-1b21-5782-86a2-8a90b8121b34" 13194139535363 true] [17592186345916 1034 "x=-2,3" 13194139535363 true] [17592186345916 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535363 true] [17592186345916 1111 #uuid "7005cb60-66a4-5de3-8d19-4ad97561c698" 13194139535363 true] [17592186345917 1034 "x=-2" 13194139535363 true] [17592186345917 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535363 true] [17592186345917 1111 #uuid "6d6d49e4-f011-5f80-a12a-4a933c6237a3" 13194139535363 true] [17592186345918 1017 #edb/ref 17592186345919 13194139535363 true] [17592186345918 1089 "q-107075" 13194139535363 true] [17592186345918 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535363 true] [17592186345918 1100 "Find the vertical asymptotes of $f(x)=\\frac{5}{2x}+\\frac{3}{4x}.$" 13194139535363 true] [17592186345918 1113 #uuid "9bd3afc4-6ef3-52a7-9d8b-591f71cdd447" 13194139535363 true] [17592186345918 1145 "First, let's put the two terms over a common denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{2x}+\\frac{3}{4x} & =\\frac{5(2)+3}{4x}=\\frac{13}{4x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere are no common factors in the numerator and denominator, so we proceed to set the denominator equal to zero and get\n\n$$\n4x=0\\,⟹\\,x=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vertical asymptotes are at $x=0.$" 13194139535363 true] [17592186345919 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345920 13194139535363 true] [17592186345919 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345921 13194139535363 true] [17592186345919 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345922 13194139535363 true] [17592186345919 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345923 13194139535363 true] [17592186345919 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345924 13194139535363 true] [17592186345919 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535363 true] [17592186345919 1041 "selection" 13194139535363 true] [17592186345919 1104 #edb/ref 17592186345923 13194139535363 true] [17592186345919 1110 #uuid "e619eb1a-dff4-5889-893b-fba716003d10" 13194139535363 true] [17592186345920 1034 "No vertical asymptotes" 13194139535363 true] [17592186345920 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535363 true] [17592186345920 1111 #uuid "2f183f20-972b-5974-852f-018f3b363cca" 13194139535363 true] [17592186345921 1034 "x=1" 13194139535363 true] [17592186345921 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535363 true] [17592186345921 1111 #uuid "086c9bf1-8b02-57c1-a86e-b5c780099044" 13194139535363 true] [17592186345922 1034 "x=\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139535363 true] [17592186345922 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535363 true] [17592186345922 1111 #uuid "0920d4c7-131b-56a9-9939-37c13707b9e7" 13194139535363 true] [17592186345923 1034 "x=0" 13194139535363 true] [17592186345923 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535363 true] [17592186345923 1111 #uuid "d8cf719b-1ced-52e4-a290-709d75a6a0a5" 13194139535363 true] [17592186345924 1034 "$x=0$ and $x=1$" 13194139535363 true] [17592186345924 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535363 true] [17592186345924 1111 #uuid "274e5465-cc28-5c25-8cf6-a27dd4c265f8" 13194139535363 true] [17592186345925 1017 #edb/ref 17592186345926 13194139535363 true] [17592186345925 1089 "q-339968" 13194139535363 true] [17592186345925 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535363 true] [17592186345925 1100 "The vertical asymptote of $f(x)=\\frac{8x-16}{{x}^{2}-6x+8}$ is\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}." 13194139535363 true] [17592186345925 1113 #uuid "a0ab7f79-8620-5428-92fb-a584d8a11e91" 13194139535363 true] [17592186345925 1145 "We start by factoring the function as much as possible and canceling the common factors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8x-16}{{x}^{2}-6x+8} & =\\frac{8(x-2)}{(x-2)(x-4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{8\\cancel{(x-2)}}{\\cancel{(x-2)}(x-4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{x-4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now set the denominator equal to zero:\n\n$$\nx-4=0\\,⟹\\,x=4\n$$\n\nSo the *only* vertical asymptote is at $x=4.$" 13194139535363 true] [17592186345926 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345927 13194139535363 true] [17592186345926 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535363 true] [17592186345926 1041 "field-1" 13194139535363 true] [17592186345926 1104 #edb/ref 17592186345927 13194139535363 true] [17592186345926 1110 #uuid "f020e236-c3df-53b3-886d-2d973e9d2393" 13194139535363 true] [17592186345927 1034 "4" 13194139535363 true] [17592186345927 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535363 true] [17592186345927 1111 #uuid "03d36870-f66e-531f-92f2-7c5cb21b2088" 13194139535363 true] [17592186345928 1017 #edb/ref 17592186345929 13194139535363 true] [17592186345928 1089 "q-37067" 13194139535363 true] [17592186345928 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535363 true] [17592186345928 1100 "Find the vertical asymptotes of $f(x)=\\frac{{x}^{2}-4}{2{x}^{2}+5x+2}.$" 13194139535363 true] [17592186345928 1113 #uuid "3686a814-0b2c-5876-8371-9a4c81bce6f5" 13194139535363 true] [17592186345928 1145 "We start by factoring the function as much as possible and canceling the common factors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}-4}{2{x}^{2}+5x+2} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}-{2}^{2}}{2{x}^{2}+4x+x+2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x+2)(x-2)}{2x(x+2)+(x+2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x+2)(x-2)}{(2x+1)(x+2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{(x+2)}(x-2)}{(2x+1)\\cancel{(x+2)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{x-2}{2x+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now set the denominator equal to zero:\n\n$$\n2x+1=0\\,⟹\\,x=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the *only* vertical asymptote is at $x=-\\frac{1}{2}.$" 13194139535363 true] [17592186345929 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345930 13194139535363 true] [17592186345929 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345931 13194139535363 true] [17592186345929 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345932 13194139535363 true] [17592186345929 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345933 13194139535363 true] [17592186345929 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345934 13194139535363 true] [17592186345929 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535363 true] [17592186345929 1041 "selection" 13194139535363 true] [17592186345929 1104 #edb/ref 17592186345933 13194139535363 true] [17592186345929 1110 #uuid "092be388-8063-5ad5-8200-ae4d7df3d593" 13194139535363 true] [17592186345930 1034 "x=\\frac{4}{3}" 13194139535363 true] [17592186345930 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535363 true] [17592186345930 1111 #uuid "b30b5956-7a30-5fb5-8006-df94a7778e77" 13194139535363 true] [17592186345931 1034 "$x=-\\frac{1}{2}$, $x=-2$" 13194139535363 true] [17592186345931 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535363 true] [17592186345931 1111 #uuid "7b8b6a9c-0f11-5efb-a3b1-bb0f64a10ddd" 13194139535363 true] [17592186345932 1034 "No vertical  asymptotes" 13194139535363 true] [17592186345932 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535363 true] [17592186345932 1111 #uuid "e410ab0a-4018-5a00-830b-b6d6ea8f35ac" 13194139535363 true] [17592186345933 1034 "x=-\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139535363 true] [17592186345933 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535363 true] [17592186345933 1111 #uuid "c2f41616-8934-5a1b-bc98-40d0e6b12d15" 13194139535363 true] [17592186345934 1034 "x=-2" 13194139535363 true] [17592186345934 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535363 true] [17592186345934 1111 #uuid "aba7417d-1f6e-529f-9b3d-52057e3b050f" 13194139535363 true] [17592186345935 1017 #edb/ref 17592186345936 13194139535363 true] [17592186345935 1089 "q-73015" 13194139535363 true] [17592186345935 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535363 true] [17592186345935 1100 "Find the vertical asymptotes of $f(x)=\\frac{{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}}{2x+4}.$" 13194139535363 true] [1759218634593